        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(boot-echo): keep echo guard chunking UTF-16 safe",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe boot echo guard's 80-char sliding-window chunking uses `.slice()` on UTF-16 code-unit boundaries, which can split surrogate pairs and produce misaligned chunks near emoji/CJK characters.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSurrogate pairs split by raw code-unit slicing produce orphaned high/low surrogates in the chunk set, potentially causing echo matching to misalign near supplementary-plane characters.\n\n## Code Change\n\nThe original `sliceUtf16SafeMinLen` retried only +1 extra character when `sliceUtf16Safe` trimmed the end for a surrogate pair. But `sliceUtf16Safe` can trim up to 1 char from the start (low-surrogate skip) and up to 1 from the end (high-surrogate skip), so the range may need extending by up to 2 to guarantee the minimum window length. The fix retries up to +2.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers whose prompts contain emoji or CJK characters near an echo-match boundary may see incorrect echo detection behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n```\n$ script -q -c \"node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/gateway/boot-echo-guard.test.ts\"\n\n RUN  v4.1.10 /home/lizeyu/workspace/openclaw\n\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  6 passed (6)\n   Start at  21:12:41\n   Duration  430ms\n```\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations",
